"to the corresponding marker:"
msgstr "次は、辞書を使ってユニットに割り当てた 'minimap_icon' タグを対応するマーカーにマッピングします："

#: ui/minimap.md
msgid ""
"If there is a `player`, we'll first rotate the player marker to match the "
"player's heading. Since our `PlayerMarker` sprite points upwards rather than "
"along the `x` axis, we must add 90 degrees:"
msgstr ""
"如果存在玩家，首先我们会根据玩家的方向旋转玩家标记。由于我们的 PlayerMarker 图灵向上方而不是沿 x 轴指向，因此需要增加 90 度："

#: ui/minimap.md
msgid ""
"To fix this, after calculating `obj_pos`, but before setting the marker's "
"position, clamp it to the grid's rectangle:"
msgstr "この問題を解決するには、`obj_pos` を計算した後、マーカーの位置を設定する前に、その値をグリッドの矩形範囲にクリップしてください："

#: ui/minimap.md
msgid ""
"Add each item that you want to appear on the minimap to a group named "
"\"minimap_objects\". In each object's script, assign it a `minimap_icon` "
"property:"
msgstr ""
"ミニマップ上に表示させたい各アイテムを「minimap_objects」というグループに追加してください。各オブジェクトのスクリプトにおいて、`minima"
"p_icon`プロパティを適切に設定します："

#: ui/minimap.md
msgid ""
"We'll also create markers for every game object (using the "
"\"minimap_objects\" group) by duplicating the matching marker node and tying "
"the marker to the object via the `markers` dictionary:"
msgstr ""
"```python\n"
"from bpy import context, data, ops\n"
"import copy\n"
"\n"
"def create_game_object_markers():\n"
"    # Get the current active scene\n"
"    scene = context.scene\n"
"\n"
"    # Iterate over each game object in the scene\n"
"    for obj in scene.objects:\n"
"        if obj.type == 'GAMEOBJECT':\n"
"            # Create a marker node with the same name as the game object\n"
"            marker_node = bpy.data.nodes.new('ShaderNodeGroup')\n"
"            marker_node.name = obj.name\n"
"\n"
"            # Ensure the marker is properly linked to the game object\n"
"            obj.node_tree.nodes[-1].use_shader_node_group = True\n"
"            obj.node_tree.nodes[-1].group_path = \"#\" + obj.name\n"
"\n"
"            # Store the marker in the dictionary for quick access\n"
"            markers[obj] = marker_node\n"
"```"

