#: Math/interpolation.md
msgid ""
"The following example moves a Sprite node towards the mouse click position. "
"Each frame the node moves 10% of the way to the target. This results in an "
"\"approach\" effect, where the object's speed becomes slower the closer it "
"gets to the target."
msgstr ""
"以下の例では、スプライトノードをマウスクリック位置に移動させています。各フレームごとにノードは目標位置まで10%ずつ近づきます。これにより、オブジェクトが近"
"づくにつれて速度が徐々に減速する「接近」効果が得られます。"

#: Math/interpolation.md
msgid ""
"You can animate a node's properties with `lerp()`. For example, if you divide "
"the elapsed time by the desired duration, you'll get a value between zero and "
"one you can use to alter a property smoothly over time. This script scales a "
"sprite up to five times its starting size while fading it out (using "
"`modulate.a`) over two seconds:"
msgstr ""
"```javascript\n"
"const elapsedTime = Time.deltaTime;\n"
"const duration = 0.5; // 2秒のアニメーション期間\n"
"\n"
"function lerpScaleAndFade(node, startSize, endSize) {\n"
"    let scaleFactor = Mathf.Lerp(startSize, endSize, elapsedTime / "
"duration);\n"
"    node.scale = Vector3.one * scaleFactor;\n"
"\n"
"    // 2秒間かけて徐々に透明化（不透明度0〜1）\n"
"    const fadeDuration = 0.2; // 1秒のフェード期間\n"
"    const currentFadeValue = Mathf.Lerp(0, 1, elapsedTime / fadeDuration);\n"
"    node.modulate.a = Mathf.LerpAmplitude(currentFadeValue, startSize, "
"endSize);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"// 2秒間かけてスプライトを5倍に拡大しながら徐々に透明化\n"
"lerpScaleAndFade(\"MySprite\", 1.0, 5.0);\n"
"```"

